 "no_horizontal_rules": "MEASURED ON THIS IMAGE, and it is the same finding the continuation sheets carry: the leaf has NO horizontal ruled lines inside the body. A row-darkness profile taken across the empty free-coloured block finds two strong rules on the leaf \u2014 under the printed heading and above the enumerator's footer \u2014 and nothing between them. The printed form rules this page vertically only, so every row assignment comes from the enumerator's own ink. On a LEFT sheet that is cheap rather than hard, because every line carries a name: the name column's ink is the row index, and each cell is then assigned to the nearest name.",
