 "reconciliation": "EVERY column the sheet carries a printed total for closes exactly. Nine male columns (16, 10, 7, 6, 28, 19, 5, 1, 1) and nine female columns (14, 12, 9, 10, 22, 17, 2, 1, 1) were summed from the read cells and compared with the enumerator's own footing: eighteen of eighteen agree, residual zero on every one. Two readings were changed BY that check rather than to satisfy it, and both are recorded here because a closure that hides its corrections is worth nothing: the males 20-under-30 footing was first read as 25 from a reduced overview and is 28 at magnification (the second glyph is an 8 whose two bowls close, not a 5 whose top bar is separate \u2014 the sheet's own 5 stands two cells to the right for comparison), and the free-white under-5 female column needed two `2`s at lines 27 and 30 that a component filter had dropped as over-tall, which the column's shortfall of 4 is what found. Three ink specks are recorded as specks and not as entries \u2014 one in the female 60-under-70 column at line 3, one in the female 80-under-90 column at line 20, and one rule fragment in the female 10-under-15 column at line 21 \u2014 and the closure is the reason: every column they stand in either closes without them or is printed blank.",
